Borrowed from {{bor|da|en|event}}, from {{der|da|frm|event}}, from {{der|da|la|ēventus||an event, occurrence}}, from {{m|la|ēveniō||to happen, to fall out, to come out}}, from {{m|la|ē||out of, from}}, short form of {{m|la|ex}} + {{m|la|veniō||come}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|da|/ɛˈvɛnt/}}

===Noun===
{{da-noun}}

# An {{l|en|event}}, a prearranged social activity (function, etc.).
#: {{ux|da|Det var et stort '''event''' i Stockholmsmessen idag.|There was a big '''event''' in the Stockholm fair today.}}

====Declension====
{{rfinfl|da}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|da|begivenhed}}

